WebDAV Filing
-------------

An ESPHome external component that serves WebDAV from an SD card. Supported
filesystems are FAT and ext2.

Prepare FAT or ext2 on a host first; ext2 volumes with host-default inode
counts are supported and use PSRAM for metadata when present. The firmware
never formats or provisions storage.


CONFIGURATION

All component settings are here with their defaults. REQUIRED marks settings
that must be checked or changed for the board and card.

    webdav_filing:
      http:
        port: 8080                          # default
        base_path: /                        # default; use /dav or similar
        # auth:                             # optional; omit to disable auth
        #   type: digest                    # default; digest or basic
        #   username: !secret dav_username  # REQUIRED with auth
        #   password: !secret dav_password  # REQUIRED with auth; hidden in config dumps
      storage:
        sd:
          bus: spi              # default; REQUIRED: sdmmc for SDMMC wiring
          # SPI pins. REQUIRED: set these if your board is not VSPI.
          clk_pin: 18           # default for spi
          miso_pin: 19          # default for spi
          mosi_pin: 23          # default for spi
          cs_pin: 5             # default for spi
          # SDMMC pins. Use these instead when bus: sdmmc.
          # REQUIRED: set these if your board is not Waveshare P4.
          # clk_pin: 43         # default for sdmmc
          # cmd_pin: 44         # default for sdmmc
          # d0_pin: 39          # default for sdmmc
          # d1_pin: 40          # default for sdmmc, width 4
          # d2_pin: 41          # default for sdmmc, width 4
          # d3_pin: 42          # default for sdmmc, width 4
          frequency: 4MHz       # default
          slot: 0               # default
          width: 4              # default
          pwr_ldo_channel: 0    # default; REQUIRED: 4 on Waveshare P4

Required to check: the SD pins for your wiring, bus: sdmmc for SDMMC wiring,
and pwr_ldo_channel: 4 on Waveshare P4. Old flat keys and the old server bucket
are rejected. http.base_path is only an HTTP prefix; the WebDAV root stays /.
/fs/name is a legacy alias inside the prefix.


STORAGE

Every FAT and ext2 volume on the card is mounted automatically. With one
volume it is served at the share root. With several volumes they appear as
top-level directories such as /fatdata/ and /davdata/; the virtual root is
read-only and COPY/MOVE cannot cross volumes. The ext2 /lost+found directory
is hidden from the share. ext2 uses fixed-size metadata caches, so
host-formatted volumes up to 2 TiB with 4 KiB blocks are supported without
RAM scaling by group count.


AUTHENTICATION

Authentication is optional and goes under http. One account is supported. Put
the username and password in secrets.yaml and reference them with !secret; the
password is marked sensitive so config dumps and logs do not print it. Digest
is the default; use type: basic only if a client cannot handle Digest. Music
Assistant sends Basic credentials only, so it needs type: basic. There is no
TLS, so keep the share on a trusted LAN. Credentials in a URL such as
http://user:pass@host/ are not used; send them through the Authorization
header.


SECRETS

Copy secrets.example.yaml to secrets.yaml and replace the placeholders. The
dav_username and dav_password keys are only needed when http.auth is enabled.


EXAMPLES

example.yaml is the generic ESP32 SPI example. example-p4.yaml is a
board-specific reference for Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6 rev1.3. Configurations in
tests/ are emulator and test fixtures, not user examples.

The published repository is github.com/ganehag/fileserver_esphome. In Home
Assistant, replace the local source in an example with the pinned git source
shown in its comment.


